ligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the fact that ${x}^{2}>0.$\n\nHence, ${f}^{″}(x)>0$ when $x>1.$ So the graph is concave up on the interval $(1,\\infty ).$\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is concave down when ${f}^{″}(x)<0.$ By similar reasoning to before, this leads to the inequality ${x}^{3}-1<0,$ which has the solution $(0,1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \" II only.\"" 13194139534537 true] [17592186293702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293703 13194139534537 true] [17592186293702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293704 13194139534537 true] [17592186293702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293705 13194139534537 true] [17592186293702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293706 13194139534537 true] [17592186293702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293707 13194139534537 true] [17592186293702 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534537 true] [17592186293702 1041 "selection" 13194139534537 true] [17592186293702 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293707 13194139534537 true] [17592186293702 1110 #uuid "5f1e316f-78a1-538e-a241-00deb8b4f4bf" 13194139534537 true] [17592186293703 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534537 true] [17592186293703 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534537 true] [17592186293703 1111 #uuid "ae1c2967-fe66-5164-8106-1c48cf85e021" 13194139534537 true] [17592186293704 1034 "I only" 13194139534537 true] [17592186293704 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534537 true] [17592186293704 1111 #uuid "98153d91-ae04-593a-acd3-4afb60a74acf" 13194139534537 true] [17592186293705 1034 "III only" 13194139534537 true] [17592186293705 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534537 true] [17592186293705 1111 #uuid "5bbd670c-e59b-51e5-8b48-a6c89b0f0fed" 13194139534537 true] [17592186293706 1034 "None of the statements are true." 13194139534537 true] [17592186293706 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534537 true] [17592186293706 1111 #uuid "a0ab2773-bf4c-52c2-ba6c-89081c9bdd5a" 13194139534537 true] [17592186293707 1034 "II only" 13194139534537 true] [17592186293707 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534537 true] [17592186293707 1111 #uuid "a91